-- Rollback for 0074_purge_unentitled_brief_and_followup_rows.sql
--
-- Not restorable, and deliberately not faked.
--
-- The forward migration deletes rows; nothing captures them first. A
-- rollback that recreated them would have to invent subjects it never
-- had, and a rollback that silently did nothing while claiming to
-- restore is worse than one that says so.
--
-- Reverting is also not something anyone should want. These rows were
-- Gmail subject lines collected for workspaces that never had Brief or
-- Follow-ups — the point of deleting them is that we should not hold
-- them. Both producers are gated as of PR #621, so nothing refills the
-- tables for unentitled workspaces, and entitled workspaces were never
-- touched: their Brief regenerates nightly regardless.
SELECT 1;
